# CHANGES.log

## 2026-06-18 — Analyse workspace critical audit + reconciliation

Goal: terminate noise, keep only defensible signal; every feature must change a real
decision for the better. Methodology: Claude (architect) owned the audit + logic spec
+ review; Codex (executor) implemented the Scrap reframe + wrote the Vitest suite.
See docs/ANALYSE_PRD.md §0 (Goal & Methodology) and §1–§4 for equations/provenance.

Audit findings acted on:
- Scrap is DIFFUSE, not Pareto (32/94 products = 80%, top is ~9.7%) → killed the
  "vital few" framing; relabelled the concentration card; Pareto caption states the
  honest top-10 cumulative ("scrap is diffuse").
- The P25 "recoverable" was an arbitrary vanity number → replaced (see v2 below).
- Removed cosmetic driver() "likely lever" guesses.
- Scrap data relabelled line-level (Extrusion Line 1 / Machines 01 & 03), not MC01.
- Planner: false "Rate variability: measured from history" label → adjustable estimate
  (rateCv), wired through Monte-Carlo + levers. TOU made season-honest (summer/winter
  toggle; winter bands flat → lever only pays in summer). Default dataset → pilot (real).
- Delivery View reconciled to the system: MC01 single machine (was 3 + "add a machine"
  recommendation), 16 h/day, pilot/demo toggle defaulting to real.
- Dead code removed from productionModel.ts (planStrategy, planAll, buildSchedule,
  monteCarloFit, EPQ/MTS-MTO strategy engine).

Tests (Codex, src/lib/__tests__/productionModel.test.ts, Vitest): scheduleOrders
single-lane + priority-first + bounded steady-state + additive scrap; monteCarloOrders
bounded probs + sorted samples; scrap Pareto cumulative monotonic & first-80 index
(locks out the cumulative-line bug); recoverable excludes low-sample; dead exports
absent; source guards. Result: 6/6 pass. tsc clean. npm run build PROVENANCE CHECK PASSED.

## 2026-06-18 — Scrap Focus v2 (hard-pass follow-up)

Hard review of the live numbers found the gap-to-plant-average "recoverable" was
trivial (213 OMR/yr, 1.6% of loss) and hid the biggest, volume-driven losses
(PR110 #2 by scrap got zero recommendation because its rate was already below avg).

Fix (architect spec, Codex executed + tested):
- Per-product target -> each product's OWN best-demonstrated reject (its P25 across
  its own shift records; added as bestRejectOwn to scrapCatalog.json, null when <5
  records). Recoverable now 3,208 OMR/yr; top recs PR110 (~850) and DR152 (~810).
- Added a "Plant-wide lever" card: every 0.5 pp of line reject ~ 2,438 OMR/yr (1 pp
  ~ 4,876) — the honest headline for diffuse scrap. Replaced the Concentration card.
- Pareto + ranking now well-measured-only (24 of 94); banner states 5,472 OMR sits
  in 70 low-sample products excluded from ranking until more data.
- Table shows "Best %"; recs/drilldown read "reject X% -> your best Y% -> save Z".

Tests extended: recoverable uses bestRejectOwn & excludes null/low-sample; bestRejectOwn
non-null iff samples>=5; plant-wide sensitivity = 0.005*sum(demand*kg)*price; well-measured
Pareto cumulative monotonic & <=100. Result: 9/9 pass. tsc clean. build provenance passed.

