## 2026-06-19 — Energy intensity (Planner) + Scrap diagnostic drill-down

Founder asked: make scrap recs prescriptive (where/why, not just "you have a problem"),
and add kWh/kg to the Planner. Data check: records have NO process settings
(temp/speed/vacuum/material lot), remarks_raw empty, color/class/wall constant per
product — so the ONLY within-product cause dimensions are shift (1 vs 2) and month.
The quantified "do Z -> cut X" engine is a DATA gap (process logging), not a hard model;
extrusion reject is process-empirical, not closed-form physics. Built the honest
diagnostic we CAN support today.

Architect data prep: added per-product shift1Reject, shift2Reject, monthly[] to
scrapCatalog.json (from shift1/2 scrap split + monthly aggregation) + types.

Implemented (Codex + tests):
- Planner: `energyIntensityKwhPerKg` helper; "kWh/kg" column in run-by-run detail;
  "Energy intensity — kWh per kg by product" bar chart (run energy only).
- Scrap drill-down "Where the loss is": shift-1 vs shift-2 reject with worse-shift
  callout (>=0.5pp); monthly trend sparkline (best vs worst month, capability-vs-
  consistency framing, bestRejectOwn marked); honest footer that exact-knob attribution
  needs run-level process logging.

Tests: 15/15 (energyIntensityKwhPerKg value+zero-guard; diagnostic fields present +
DU203 shift2>shift1 + monthly bounds; source guards). tsc clean; build provenance passed.

## 2026-06-19 — kWh/kg KPI on the decision hub (measured, line-level)

Founder wanted kWh/kg as a flagship KPI, benchmarked. Data check killed the per-product
version honestly: 0/94 products have a run rate, and there is NO per-machine/per-product
energy meter — only monthly whole-factory bills + MC01 production. Extruder specific energy
is also ~constant per material, so per-product variance is tiny; the real signal is
line×time utilization. Building 94 per-product kWh/kg would be fabrication.

Built instead (measured, honest): line×month kWh/kg from nizwa bills ÷ MC01 production
(energyKpi.json + energyKpi.ts). Range 1.14 (Mar-2026, best) .. 13.59 (Dec-2025, near-idle)
— electricity is ~fixed (~250-300k kWh/mo) so kWh/kg is a UTILIZATION metric. Added as the
3rd decision card on the Analyse hub: latest kWh/kg + best/worst benchmark + monthly
sparkline (best month highlighted) + driver caption + honest "factory bills, not yet
sub-metered" footnote. Per-product kWh/kg is now a headline data-request item.

Tests: 17/17 (energyKpi sanity: kwhPerKg>0, best=min, worst=max; hub source guard). tsc
clean; build provenance passed.

## 2026-06-19 — Per-product kWh/kg PLACEHOLDER (swap-ready) in Scrap Focus

Founder wants per-product kWh/kg visualised now (table + graph); real data later. Honest
constraint: 0/94 have a run rate, no per-machine energy meter (only 2 product Excels on
Desktop), so a real per-product kWh/kg is impossible today and a naive all-94 estimate is
confounded (reflects throughput, not efficiency). Built a clearly-labelled PLACEHOLDER.

Swap-ready as a worked example of the live-data pattern:
- Data: per-product kwhPerKgPlaceholder (nameplate 75kW x16h / real mean daily output,
  clamped 0.25-1.10; deterministic) + meta kwhPerKgProvenance:'PLACEHOLDER' + kwhPerKgNote.
- UI: "kWh/kg*" table column + "Energy intensity - kWh/kg by product" bar chart, both with
  an amber PLACEHOLDER badge GATED on meta.kwhPerKgProvenance === 'PLACEHOLDER'. When
  sub-metering arrives: refill the field + flip the flag to 'measured' -> badge auto-hides,
  zero component change.

Integration architecture (for the record): each data domain = generated JSON + typed
wrapper + provenance meta; components depend on type+flag, not source, so live data =
regenerate JSON + flip flag. Live gaps: orders generated in-component (extract to a data
provider = #1 seam); no ingestion/API layer (batch JSON); telemetry batch not streaming;
provenance per-dataset not per-field; heavy compute -> server tier at scale.

Tests: 19/19 (placeholder finite>0 + flag=PLACEHOLDER; gated-badge source guard). tsc
clean; build provenance passed.

