## 2026-06-21 — Analyse v2 P0: Startup Ledger + startup-first Planner + root-cause taxonomy

Driven by the validated ERP finding that the dominant controllable loss is startup/purge
scrap (first-day run scraps ~3x continuation; small runs ~4x; both are the same startup-only
run). Reorganises the Analyse workspace around startups.

Engine (productionModel.ts): new `computeStartupLedger()` + `StartupLedger` type +
`MIN_ECONOMIC_RUN_KG` (3000, ESTIMATE); `runKg`/`isSubEconomic` added to `OrderItem`
(strict `<` boundary); `rootCauseForOrderItem()` + 5-tag `RootCause` union with fixed
priority (Cold-start > Startup overload > Sub-economic > Due-date compression > Pure
capacity). `startups = familyChanges + diameterChanges + 1` (first run's setupType is
'none'); `startupScrapKg` reused as single source of truth.

UI: Planner verdict card reframed startup-first (OTIF retained, secondary); new Startup
Ledger card; "This plan (estimated)" 4-tile KPI strip; per-run startup?/sub-economic
flags; strategy options relabeled to manager language (mode values unchanged); TOU lever
kept but demoted. Delivery View wired to the new RootCause taxonomy. Every new number
carries an amber "estimated" chip; cold-start shown as "family-change / cold-start proxy"
(the real idle-gap cold-start arrives in P1 via startupKpis.json).

Spec: docs/CODEX_BRIEF_P0_STARTUP_LEDGER.md. Implemented by Codex; architect-reviewed
(engine semantics + honesty contract verified). Tests 36/36 pass (incl. new
ProductionPlannerPage.test.tsx); `npm run build` clean (provenance gate + tsc + Vite);
no new deps; tariffEngine.ts untouched. P1 (wire measured weekly KPIs + floor-walk) pending.

