## 2026-06-21 — Batching Advisor (action engine) on the Order Planner

Turns the startup-scrap finding into an action: proposes consolidating small same-product
orders into campaigns and quantifies save-vs-risk.

- New pure module src/features/production-planning/batchingAdvisor.ts: suggestBatches()
  + applyBatchSuggestion(). Candidates = >=2 sub-economic same-productId orders due within
  a window (default 7d); merges each into one run (qty summed, due = earliest); re-simulates
  and derives startupsSaved/scrapSavedKg/scrapSavedOmr/addedLateDays/OTIF from
  computeStartupLedger (single source of truth — reconciliation is a test). Ranks by OMR
  saved, tie-break id; feasible = addedLateDays <= 1; deterministic (no Date.now/random).
- Planner: Batching Advisor card with ranked suggestions, amber "estimated" chip + explicit
  "no kWh claimed" note, Apply(preview)+Revert, infeasible rows muted with override cost.
  energySavedKwh left as undefined placeholder.

Implemented by Codex; architect-reviewed (engine reuse + honesty contract). Tests 54/54
pass (6 files); npm run build clean (provenance gate + tsc + Vite); no new deps;
scheduleOrders/computeStartupLedger/Scrap/Delivery/tariff untouched. Spec:
docs/CODEX_BRIEF_BATCHING_ADVISOR.md.

