## 2026-06-21 — "The Week" board on the Analyse Hub (designed entry point)

A ~30-second weekly operating board atop the Analyse Hub, making startup loss the workspace's
operating language. Three zones: (1) signature **ignition tally** — the period's startups as
discrete ignition marks (cold-starts frosted ❄), count == KPI, aria-labelled; (2) four measured
KPI tiles (startups, cold-starts, scrap/startup, % sub-economic); (3) a SCENARIO "one move" =
the top Batching Advisor suggestion with an Open-in-Planner CTA (or empty state).

Design (frontend-design skill): evidence tiers made literal — measured (emerald) tally+KPIs
visually distinct from the scenario (amber/slate) one-move; teal-accented board surface; dark
mode; reduced-motion; keyboard focus on the CTA. Architect retune after review: switched from
the latest (partial) week to a **trailing 4-week window** (latest week was only 3 startups);
relabelled "Last 4 weeks (2026-W16–W19)"; startup-weighted scrap/startup. Real board: 21
startups, 3 cold, 185.4 kg/startup, 19% sub-economic.

Implemented by Codex; architect-designed + reviewed (signature + evidence-tier honesty + the
window retune). Tests 61/61 pass (9 files); npm run build clean (provenance gate + tsc + Vite);
no new deps; only AnalyseHubPage + its test changed. Spec: docs/CODEX_BRIEF_WEEKLY_BOARD.md.
